Report Guix System update state in upgrades-installed-check.

upgrades-installed-check walks a chain of per-distribution branches to decide
whether updates are available.  Add a Guix System branch (detected by
/run/current-system) before the Archlinux branch.

Guix has no metadata-index probe comparable to dnf check-update or
apt-get -s upgrade, but "updates available" for a Guix System has a precise,
cheap meaning: at least one channel in /etc/guix/channels.scm has advanced past
the commit the running system was built from.  Compare, per channel, the commit
recorded by `guix describe` against the branch head reported by
`git ls-remote` (which goes through the same http_proxy/https_proxy the updates
proxy sets, so it works in a TemplateVM with no other network).  If any channel
is behind its branch head, updates are available.  When channels.scm pins a
channel to an explicit commit, `git ls-remote` of that branch is still compared
against the recorded commit, which is correct: a pinned system reports no update
until the pin is bumped.

Falls back to "true" (no updates) only when the comparison cannot be performed
(no channels.scm, git/guix missing, or every ls-remote fails), so a transient
network failure never produces a false "updates available".

Upstream: QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux,
package-managers/upgrades-installed-check.
Status: should-upstream (adds a new distro branch alongside the existing
debian/arch/gentoo/alpine branches; other distributions are unaffected).

diff --git a/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check b/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check
index ceb3be2..1323d01 100755
--- a/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check
+++ b/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check
@@ -46,6 +46,55 @@ elif [ -e /etc/debian_version ]; then
     # shellcheck disable=SC2266
     echo "$apt_get_upgrade_output" | awk "/^Inst/{ print $2 }" | [ "$(wc -L)" -eq 0 ] && echo "true" || echo "false"
     echo "$apt_get_upgrade_output" >&2
+elif [ -e /run/current-system ]; then
+    ## Guix System
+    # "Updates available" means a channel in /etc/guix/channels.scm has
+    # advanced past the commit the running system was built from.  Compare,
+    # per channel, `guix describe` (installed) against `git ls-remote`
+    # (remote branch head).  ls-remote honours http_proxy/https_proxy, so it
+    # works in a TemplateVM whose only network is the Qubes updates proxy.
+    set -o pipefail
+    guix_bin="$(command -v guix || echo /run/current-system/profile/bin/guix)"
+    git_bin="$(command -v git || echo /run/current-system/profile/bin/git)"
+    if [ ! -x "$guix_bin" ] || [ ! -x "$git_bin" ]; then
+        # Cannot probe; assume up to date rather than nag spuriously.
+        echo "true"
+        exit_code=0
+    else
+        # Emit "name<TAB>url<TAB>branch<TAB>commit" per channel.
+        describe="$("$guix_bin" describe -f recutils 2>/dev/null | awk '
+            /^name:/    { name=$2 }
+            /^url:/     { url=$2 }
+            /^branch:/  { branch=$2 }
+            /^commit:/  { print name "\t" url "\t" branch "\t" $2 }
+        ')"
+        updates="false"
+        checked_any="false"
+        while IFS="$(printf "\t")" read -r _name url branch commit; do
+            [ -n "$url" ] || continue
+            [ -n "$branch" ] || branch="HEAD"
+            remote="$("$git_bin" ls-remote "$url" "refs/heads/$branch" 2>/dev/null | cut -f1)"
+            [ -n "$remote" ] || remote="$("$git_bin" ls-remote "$url" "$branch" 2>/dev/null | cut -f1)"
+            if [ -n "$remote" ]; then
+                checked_any="true"
+                if [ "$remote" != "$commit" ]; then
+                    updates="true"
+                fi
+            fi
+        done <<EOF
+$describe
+EOF
+        if [ "$checked_any" != "true" ]; then
+            # No channel could be probed (e.g. transient proxy failure);
+            # do not raise a false notification.
+            echo "true"
+        elif [ "$updates" = "true" ]; then
+            echo "false"
+        else
+            echo "true"
+        fi
+        exit_code=0
+    fi
 elif [ -e /etc/arch-release ]; then
     ## Archlinux
     checkupdates >/dev/null 2>&1
